      "classes": "1: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a bank.\n2: NO MATCH -- An operator is not an IT operations team.\n3: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a service desk.\n4: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a network operations centre.\n5: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a security operations centre.\n6: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes an incident response team.\n7: NO MATCH -- An alert operator is not necessarily an on-call engineer.\n8: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a service owner.\n9: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes an application owner.\n10: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a technical owner.\n11: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a business owner.\n12: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a vendor.\n13: NO MATCH -- Stakeholder communication is not a stakeholder.\n14: NO MATCH -- A critical business transaction is not a business process.\n15: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a service level objective.\n16: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes an application.\n17: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a database.\n18: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes an infrastructure component.\n19: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a server.\n20: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a virtual machine.\n21: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a container platform.\n22: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a cloud service.\n23: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a network device.\n24: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a network segment.\n25: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes an endpoint.\n26: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a storage system.\n27: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a data centre.\n28: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a site.\n29: NO MATCH -- A recovery environment is a specific kind of environment.\n30: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a data asset.\n31: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes an integration interface.\n32: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a third-party service.\n33: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a monitoring tool.\n34: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a metric.\n35: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a log source.\n36: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a security event.\n37: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a major incident.\n38: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a cybersecurity incident.\n39: NO MATCH -- A containment action is not an emergency change.\n40: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a release.\n41: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a deployment.\n42: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a runbook.\n43: NO MATCH -- No candidate denotes a business continuity plan.\n44: NO MATCH -- A verification check is not a disaster recovery test.\n45: NO MATCH -- Stakeholder communication is narrower than communication generally.\n46: MATCH 7 -- Both denote a regulatory notification concerning an incident.",
      "relationships": "1: NO MATCH -- No candidate links a Business Service to its delivery channel.\n2: MATCH 4 -- An IT Service supporting a Business Service is the reciprocal dependency.\n3: MATCH 17 -- Both say the Backup Set protects the Configuration Item.\n4: MATCH 16 -- The Recovery Plan applies to the IT Service it recovers.\n5: NO MATCH -- No candidate links a Recovery Plan to a Backup Set.\n6: NO MATCH -- No candidate says an Event is observed on a Configuration Item.\n7: NO MATCH -- No candidate relates an Event to an IT Service.\n8: MATCH 9 -- Both link the Alert to the Monitoring Rule that generates it.\n9: NO MATCH -- Being triggered by an Event differs from indicating it.\n10: NO MATCH -- Correlating an Alert into an Incident differs from opening one.\n11: MATCH 2 -- Both describe an Event being correlated into an Incident.\n12: NO MATCH -- No candidate says an Incident impacts a Business Service.\n13: NO MATCH -- Merely concerning a Configuration Item does not establish that it is affected.\n14: MATCH 10 -- Incident evidence supports the Incident.\n15: NO MATCH -- A Change being for an Incident does not establish that it resolves it.\n16: MATCH 20 -- Both describe using a Recovery Plan for the Incident.\n17: MATCH 11 -- The associated Materiality Assessment evaluates the Incident.\n18: MATCH 12 -- The associated Post Incident Review reviews the Incident.\n19: MATCH 18 -- Both say the Problem is documented as a Known Error.\n20: NO MATCH -- No candidate links a Known Error to an affected Configuration Item.\n21: NO MATCH -- Affecting a Configuration Item is broader than modifying it.\n22: NO MATCH -- No candidate links a Change to an affected IT Service.\n23: MATCH 19 -- Both say a Change implements the Corrective Action.",
